  "slug": "phenotype-biomedical-corpus-b5a5",
  "summary": "Agentic LLM systems are now reaching physical execution in biology, alongside red-teaming of their biosynthesis planning risks.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is infrastructure that lets LLM agents plan, execute and assess biological workflows. PharmAgents2 proposes an autonomous multi-agent system for end-to-end drug discovery, with knowledge extraction, parallel agent scaling and a 121-question evaluation. BioMARS 2.0 links literature-grounded protocol generation to feedback-driven culture optimization in a human-in-the-loop robotic setting. AutoDNA, the only peer-reviewed item, is an AI-native laboratory running over 11,000 steps across 20-plus instrument types for DNA synthesis, sequencing and storage. Building Barricades red-teams agentic biosynthesis planning, examining how agentic software erodes access barriers. What is new is closed-loop physical execution paired with adversarial assessment. Because three of four items are preprints, cross-system comparisons remain limited.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-11"
}
